From c8064a55f0ca8dff5700546798764e8cc15b1762 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: autoresearch <agent@localhost>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:40:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] crispasr: tensor-name prefix support so one GGUF can
 hold several models

core_gguf::try_get retries '<prefix><name>' (prefix from CRISPASR_GGUF_PREFIX or set_name_prefix), and the
new find_key() does the same for metadata. Every metadata accessor (kv_u32, kv_str, kv_str_array, ...) now
goes through it: a helper that quietly returns its default on a miss makes a namespace mistake look like a
corrupt model, which is how the first bundle attempt died with 'inconsistent hyper-parameters' (vocab_size
resolved to 0 because only the tensor lookup was prefix-aware). xasr's hparams reader uses find_key too.
